---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="RMAN Recovery"
  description="Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing recovery requirements, recovery area usage, restore points and flashback readiness."
>
  <main>
    <section class="resource-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
        <h1>RMAN <span class="hero-accent">Recovery</span></h1>
        <p>
          Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing recovery requirements, recovery
          area usage, restore points and flashback readiness.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resource-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="resource-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Check the database recovery path before you need it</h2>
          <p>
            Recovery investigations depend on knowing which files require
            recovery, which redo is available and whether the recovery area has
            enough capacity. These queries provide a practical starting point
            for reviewing recovery readiness.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-grid">
          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">01 &middot; FILE RECOVERY</div>
              <h2>Find files requiring recovery</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Identify data files that require media recovery and review the associated error and starting SCN.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    file#,
    error,
    online_status,
    change#,
    time
FROM v$recover_file
ORDER BY file#;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">02 &middot; REQUIRED REDO</div>
              <h2>Review redo needed for recovery</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review archived redo logs currently identified as required for media recovery.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    thread#,
    sequence#,
    filename,
    first_change#,
    next_change#
FROM v$recovery_log
ORDER BY
    thread#,
    sequence#;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">03 &middot; RECOVERY AREA</div>
              <h2>Review recovery area capacity</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Check fast recovery area quota, current usage, reclaimable space and file count.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    name,
    ROUND(space_limit / 1024 / 1024 / 1024, 2) AS limit_gb,
    ROUND(space_used / 1024 / 1024 / 1024, 2) AS used_gb,
    ROUND(space_reclaimable / 1024 / 1024 / 1024, 2) AS reclaimable_gb,
    number_of_files
FROM v$recovery_file_dest;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">04 &middot; SPACE USAGE</div>
              <h2>Review recovery area usage by file type</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Identify which recovery-area file types consume the available quota.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    file_type,
    ROUND(percent_space_used, 2) AS pct_used,
    ROUND(percent_space_reclaimable, 2) AS pct_reclaimable,
    number_of_files
FROM v$recovery_area_usage
ORDER BY percent_space_used DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">05 &middot; RESTORE POINTS</div>
              <h2>Review database restore points</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Check restore points, guaranteed flashback settings and storage associated with each point.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    name,
    time,
    scn,
    guarantee_flashback_database,
    storage_size,
    preserved
FROM v$restore_point
ORDER BY time DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">06 &middot; FLASHBACK WINDOW</div>
              <h2>Review the current flashback window</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review the oldest available flashback SCN and time supported by the current flashback logs.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    oldest_flashback_scn,
    oldest_flashback_time,
    retention_target,
    estimated_flashback_size
FROM v$flashback_database_log;</code></pre>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-note">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Recovery readiness depends on more than backup existence.</h2>
          <p>
            A recovery investigation should establish which files need
            recovery, which archived redo is required and whether the recovery
            area has sufficient capacity. Restore points and the available
            flashback window can provide additional recovery options when they
            are configured and maintained.
          </p>
          <p>
            Oracle documents <code>V$RECOVER_FILE</code> for files requiring
            media recovery, <code>V$RECOVERY_FILE_DEST</code> and
            <code>V$RECOVERY_AREA_USAGE</code> for fast recovery area usage,
            and <code>V$RESTORE_POINT</code> for restore point information.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/tools/backup-recovery/">
            Back to Backup &amp; Recovery
          </a>
          <a
            class="resource-actions__link"
            href="/tools/backup-recovery/backup-space/"
          >
            Read Backup Space
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll(".resource-block pre").forEach((pre) => {
    const button = document.createElement("button");
    button.type = "button";
    button.className = "resource-copy-button";
    button.textContent = "Copy";
    button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy SQL");

    pre.style.position = "relative";
    button.style.position = "absolute";
    button.style.top = "10px";
    button.style.right = "10px";
    button.style.padding = "5px 9px";
    button.style.border = "1px solid #d1d5db";
    button.style.borderRadius = "5px";
    button.style.background = "#ffffff";
    button.style.color = "#374151";
    button.style.fontFamily = "inherit";
    button.style.fontSize = "0.75rem";
    button.style.cursor = "pointer";
    button.style.zIndex = "2";

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const code = pre.querySelector("code");
      if (!code) return;

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent || "");
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      } catch {
        button.textContent = "Copy failed";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      }
    });

    pre.appendChild(button);
  });
</script>

<style>
  .resource-hero {
    padding-top: 82px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .resource-hero h1 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 72px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .resource-hero .hero-accent {
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .resource-hero > .container > p:last-child {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .resource-section {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }

  .resource-intro {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .resource-intro .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .resource-intro h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .resource-intro p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .resource-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 22px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .resource-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    height: 560px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 30px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 18px;
    transition:
      border-color 0.22s ease,
      box-shadow 0.22s ease,
      transform 0.22s ease;
  }

  .resource-block:hover {
    border-color: #d8dce1;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(17, 29, 44, 0.06);
    transform: translateY(-3px);
  }

  .resource-block__header {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .resource-block__label {
    margin-bottom: 9px;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .resource-block h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .resource-block__description {
    min-height: 48px;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .resource-block pre {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-height: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 22px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    overflow-y: auto;
    white-space: pre;
    background: #2f353d;
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: #f3f4f6;
    font-family:
      "Cascadia Code",
      "Consolas",
      "Courier New",
      monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .resource-block code {
    font-family: inherit;
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .resource-copy-button {
    position: absolute;
    top: 10px;
    right: 10px;
    padding: 5px 9px;
    border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #374151;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .resource-copy-button:hover {
    background: #f3f4f6;
  }

  .resource-note {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding: 30px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background: #f7f8fa;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .resource-note .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .resource-note h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .resource-note p:not(.eyebrow) {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .resource-note p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .resource-note code {
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #eef0f2;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family:
      "Cascadia Code",
      "Consolas",
      "Courier New",
      monospace;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }

  .resource-actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .resource-actions__link {
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .resource-actions__link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .resource-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .resource-hero {
      padding-top: 58px;
      padding-bottom: 54px;
    }

    .resource-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(38px, 12vw, 54px);
    }

    .resource-section {
      padding-top: 44px;
      padding-bottom: 56px;
    }

    .resource-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 16px;
    }

    .resource-block {
      height: 520px;
      padding: 22px;
      border-radius: 16px;
    }

    .resource-block__description {
      min-height: 0;
    }

    .resource-block pre {
      padding: 18px;
      font-size: 12px;
    }

    .resource-note {
      padding: 22px;
      border-radius: 16px;
    }

    .resource-actions {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
